\label{conj1}
$\xi_{g,1}$ is the unique closed, embedded minimal surface $M$ of genus $g\geq 2$ in $\esf^3$ whose isometry group contains a Klein subgroup $\Z_2\times \Z_2=\langle \phi,\phi'\rangle$ such that $\phi,\phi'$ are reflections across orthogonal spheres $S,S'\subset \esf^3$ (orientation-reversing on $M$), the closures $\Omega^+,\Omega^-=\phi(\Omega^+)$ of the components of $M\setminus S$
have genus zero, and all the boundary components of $\partial \Omega^+=\partial \Omega^-$ intersect the great circle $S\cap S'$.
\end{conjecture}

